   266	  parser and month-limit table. It checked every two-digit month/day pair for
   267	  years `0000`, `2000`, and `9999`, plus malformed and Unicode-digit cases:
   268	  30,010 inputs, zero mismatches.
   269	- Parsed KORE equality connects the AST constant used in proof to the generated
   270	  `solution.mpy`.
   271	
   272	These finite checks support adequacy and identity; the universal result comes
   273	from the two `#Top` proof commands.
   274	
   275	## Excluded behavior
   276	
   277	- Arguments that are not strings.
   278	- Full CPython behavior outside the supplied MPY subset.
   279	- Side effects in the final module-scope map, which are setup artifacts and not
   280	  observable in the HumanEval contract.
   281	- Termination as a separately proved liveness theorem; the reported K theorem
   282	  is partial correctness, although this implementation is loop-free.
